      "en": "> **Internal Note — Cross-Border Case File Exchange Pilot**\n> *Interinstitutional Digital Cooperation Unit*\n>\n> Between January and June, three national administrations and one EU agency piloted the electronic exchange of case files that had previously been sent by post or as unstructured email attachments. In the pilot's first phase, 40% of files required manual reformatting on arrival because sending and receiving systems used incompatible formats, adding an average of 6 working days to case handling time.\n>\n> In the pilot's second phase, participants adopted a shared data standard, the \"Common Exchange Format v2,\" for all new files. Manual reformatting fell to under 5% of files, and the added handling time fell to an average of 1 working day. Participant feedback was strongly positive, though two participants noted that adopting the standard required a one-off investment in updating their local systems.\n>\n> The pilot team's closing report recommends extending use of the Common Exchange Format v2 to all participating bodies, coordinated through a new working group, but flags that a wider rollout would require a budget line and formal sign-off, as some administrations will need technical support to make the switch.\n\n**Task:** You are a policy officer in the Interinstitutional Digital Cooperation Unit. Draft a briefing note (around 250 words) for your Director, who has not read the full pilot report, summarising the findings and recommending whether and how to proceed.",
